   "text": "That was the simulation — this is your coach. Textbook BEC defense: you never let urgency override verification, you asked for a documentable reference number, and you refused to even hear the new bank details on an inbound call — that's exactly right, because writing them down is already half the compromise. One nit: name the callback step before they object, so it reads as policy rather than stonewalling."
